.SS "void sc_finalize (void)"

.PP
Unregisters all packages, runs the memory check, removes the signal handlers and resets sc_identifier and sc_root_*\&. This function aborts on any inconsistency found unless the global variable default_abort_mismatch is false\&. Function is optional if memory cleanliness is no concern\&. This function does not require sc_init to be called first\&. In any case it makes \fBsc_is_initialized\fP return false\&. 
.PP
\fBExamples\fP
.in +1c
\fBoptions\&.c\fP\&.
.SS "int sc_finalize_noabort (void)"

.PP
Unregisters all packages, runs the memory check, removes the signal handlers and resets sc_identifier and sc_root_*\&. This function never aborts but returns the number of errors encountered\&. Function is optional if memory cleanliness is no concern\&. This function does not require sc_init to be called first\&. In any case it makes \fBsc_is_initialized\fP return false\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
0 when everything is consistent, nonzero otherwise\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int sc_get_package_id (void)"

