.SS "void sc_snprintf (char * str, size_t size, const char * format,  \&.\&.\&.)"

.PP
Wrap the system snprintf function, allowing for truncation\&. The snprintf function may truncate the string written to the specified length\&. In some cases, compilers warn when this may occur\&. Here this is permitted behavior and we avoid the warning\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstr\fP Buffer of length at least \fIsize\fP\&. On output, not touched if NULL or \fIsize\fP == 0\&. Otherwise, '' on snprintf error or the proper result\&. The proper result is padded on the right with '\\0' if the allocation length of the string that is defined by \fIformat\fP is shorter than \fIsize\fP\&. 
.br
\fIsize\fP Allocation length of \fIstr\fP\&. 
.br
\fIformat\fP Format string as in man (3) snprintf\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sc_strcopy (char * dest, size_t size, const char * src)"

.PP
Provide a string copy function\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdest\fP Buffer of length at least \fIsize\fP\&. On output, not touched if NULL or \fIsize\fP == 0\&. Otherwise, \fIsrc\fP is copied to \fIdest\fP and \fIdest\fP is padded with '\\0' from the right if strlen (src) < size - 1\&. 
.br
\fIsize\fP Allocation length of \fIdest\fP\&. 
.br
\fIsrc\fP Null-terminated string\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Equivalent to \fBsc_snprintf\fP (dest, size, '%s', src)\&. 
.RE
.PP

